review_comments:
@afxefx you're pretty much spot on - thanks for adding a more thorough explanation.

pyecobee just blindly sends what it's given to the ecobee API, so your intuition is correct - that code block makes no sense, would never have worked, and so I removed it as part of this change (in addition to the fact that it's now also entirely inaccessible due to the newly-added preset mode validation).

I considered expanding the ecobee HA service with an optional hold type parameter, but I think that creates more confusion than it's worth (by deviating from the base `Climate` component) and would create the need to handle a variety of preset + hold duration pairs, many of which don't make sense. Realistically, it seems the only thing that users want is an indefinite away hold, so this simpler approach felt better to me.

@gjohansson-ST please pay careful attention to the casing of the preset names ("away" vs "Away") in the PR description - I believe it makes sense. I can add "lowercase" and "capitalized" notations in the description if you think that would be helpful.
